    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1381">

                <pb facs="0918" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/225.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Hamm to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Arrived Torreon last Monday. Everything is still chaotic. In several interviews
                    with Commander in Chief he has promised to protect all foreign property with the
                    exception of Spaniards towards whom and their interests he is absolutely
                    uncompromising. States all Spaniards must leave sections of the Republic under
                    his control. I made especial plea for the Durango Spaniards which was unheeded.
                    A great many flagrant cases confiscation abandoned Spanish property already
                    occurred in Torreon and vicinity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamm</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
